W("Reference to context: 'You have been bored!' The fat man chuckled to himself. (i) Who says this? (ii) Why does he chuckle? (iii) Is Fowler really bored?", 3, "(i) Ausable. (1) (ii) He is amused at Fowler's disappointment and perhaps because he knows what is soon to happen. (1) (iii) Not for long: the lights come on and Fowler has 'his first authentic thrill of the day'. (1)", "M"),
