W("Extract-based: 'Ausable moved to an armchair and sat down heavily. \"I'm going to raise the devil with the management this time, and you can bet on it,\" he said grimly. \"This is the second time in a month that somebody has got into my room through that nuisance of a balcony!\"' (i) Why does he sit down? (ii) How does his tone help the plan? (iii) What lie is planted? (iv) Which words show he is acting?", 4, "(i) To appear tired and unafraid; it also keeps him calm. (1) (ii) His grim, irritated tone makes the complaint sound natural and real. (1) (iii) That a balcony runs outside his window. (1) (iv) 'with extreme irritation' / 'moodily' / 'grimly'; he pretends anger instead of fear. (1)", "H"),
W("Extract-based: '\"Send them away!\" he warned. \"I will wait on the balcony. Send them away or I'll shoot and take my chances!\"' (i) Who says this? (ii) Why is Max afraid? (iii) What is the dramatic irony here? (iv) What does Max do next?", 4, "(i) Max. (1) (ii) He thinks the police outside will shoot. (1) (iii) The reader later learns there is no balcony; Max goes to wait where nothing exists. (1) (iv) He backs towards the window, swings his legs over the sill and drops, screaming. (1)", "H"),
W("'How does Ausable manage to make Max believe that there is a balcony attached to his room? What makes it a convincing story?' Answer in about 100 words.", 5, "Ausable invents a balcony with natural details: the room used to be part of a large unit, the next room was the living room, the balcony extends under his window and can be reached from an empty room two doors down, and the management promised but failed to block it. He repeats it as an annoyance ('second time in a month'), which sounds true. Max has no reason to doubt it because he got in by passkey and does not know the hotel. The window is dark at night, so he cannot check. (5; content 3, expression 2)", "H"),
W("'When do you think Ausable thought up his plan for getting rid of Max? Did he work it out from the beginning or make it up as events happened?' Give your view in about 100 words.", 5, "Probably he built part of it before and part as events unfolded. He had ordered a drink for his return, which Henry brought, and told the police-check story; the 'police' knock turned out to be Henry, which suggests the plan was ready. However, the balcony story looks improvised once Max mentioned the passkey and Fowler glanced at the window. So he prepared in general but used events cleverly: a mix of preparation and presence of mind. (5; content 3, expression 2)", "H"),
W("'Ausable shows great presence of mind.' Explain what the term means and give two examples, from the story and from life.", 4, "Presence of mind is the ability to think quickly and act calmly and wisely in danger or surprise. In the story, Ausable stays calm before the gun and invents a balcony. In life, a boy who sees a small kitchen fire may switch off the gas and cover the pan with a lid instead of panicking. (4)", "H"),
W("Why does Ausable let Max discover that the knock is from 'police'? What does he gain by it? Write a short paragraph (about 80 words).", 4, "The 'police' knock makes Max panic and makes him look for a way out. Ausable had earlier described the balcony, so Max chooses it. Ausable gains time and safety without a struggle, and he does not himself use violence. Instead of defying the gun, he uses Max's fear and ignorance. (4)", "H"),
W("Do you think Ausable's trick was justified, given that Max fell from a sixth-floor window? Discuss in about 100 words.", 5, "Some may say it was justified: Max was an armed intruder who threatened Ausable and Fowler and wanted a secret report that could affect history; Ausable had no weapon and no other defence. His words only suggested a way out, and Max chose to jump. Others may argue that an invented balcony led to a death and that arrest would have been better. Perhaps it is best viewed as self-defence in the fiction of a spy story. (5; content 3, expression 2)", "H", wp=False),
W("Case study: A man comes into Rekha's shop in Jaipur at closing time and demands the cash box. The shop's door is open to a busy road. Using Ausable's example (without any violence), suggest what Rekha might do to stay safe, and explain the quality she needs.", 5, "She should stay calm and speak steadily, perhaps say that she will fetch the box and signal to a neighbour or call out as though to someone nearby, or tell him that the police patrol the street and a camera is recording; she should avoid struggle and put safety first. She needs presence of mind, supported by mental preparation. (5)", "H", wp=True),
W("Fowler appears throughout the story but says very little. What is his role? Write four points.", 4, "He is the audience through whose eyes we see events; his romantic ideas are overturned; he feels fear (jumps at the knock, goes white-faced); and his ignorance lets the reader share the surprise. (4)", "H"),
W("Write a short paragraph (about 100 words) describing the story's ending from Fowler's point of view, in the first person.", 5, "Model: I stared at the waiter as he left, my heart pounding. 'But the police...' I stammered. 'There were no police,' Ausable said, only Henry whom he was expecting. And the man on the balcony? 'There is no balcony,' said the fat man. I felt the room spin. I had wanted romance and adventure and I had seen a spy beaten by a lie. The hotel had no balcony, but this tubby American had a mind sharper than any pistol. (5; content 2, expression 2, format 1)", "H"),
W("Write a diary entry (about 100 words) by Ausable after the night of the midnight visit.", 5, "Model: It is nearly one o'clock. Max is gone, and the report is safe. Fowler left looking as if he had seen a ghost. I did not enjoy it, but I had no weapon and no choice. The balcony story worked because I had planned for such a visit; Henry arrived exactly on time with the drink. I must tell the management to repair that window. Tomorrow I shall report to my people. I hope the young writer will not write about me - or perhaps he may, in a different name. (5; content 2, expression 2, format 1)", "H"),
