 ("p", "**Extract 1:** 'Ausable did not fit any description of a secret agent Fowler had ever read.' The opening makes the reader expect an ordinary man, which will make the ending more surprising. It also pokes gentle fun at the romantic image of spies from books and films."),
 ("p", "**Extract 2:** 'It's not my balcony... It belongs to the next apartment.' Ausable gives precise details to appear natural. The lie is plausible because it explains a real fact (Max's entry) and fits a normal hotel's faults."),
